    // We test that calling withdrawAndUnwrap(amount, claim, to) will never make
    // the CLP token balance of the C contract decrease by more than `amount`.
    // We cannot read internal state, so we observe via the public clpToken() getter
    // and IERC20.balanceOf on that token address, and via calls to c.

    // To allow IERC20 calls we declare the minimal interface here by referencing the
    // ERC20 public ABI through the contract's public surface: we will call
    // IERC20(token).balanceOf(address(c)). The IERC20 interface is already present
    // in the compilation unit, so we can use it directly.

    // run inputs:
    // - amount: amount to withdrawAndUnwrap
    // - claim: whether to claim extras
    // - to: recipient address for the transfer
    // Note: this function uses msg.sender == address(this) when calling c, as required.

